  (text "five arm wires,\nsoldered" (at 33.02 43.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 122b0884-1e4f-5239-a13e-11831153fa11))
  (text "screw terminals,\nto the jacks and the ground post" (at 157.48 43.18 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 1ca24536-0ec6-52b1-a038-c550da2e000b))
  (text "How the board reads:\n- Five arm wires are soldered to J1 to J5. Each pad has a second hole beside it:\n  thread the wire through that hole first, as strain relief.\n- Left signal and left ground go to the left jack (J6).\n- Right signal and right ground go to the right jack (J8).\n- The arm shield goes to the ground post (J7). It is not joined to either channel ground on this board.\n- C1 and C2 are empty places for cartridge loading capacitors.\n  Leave them empty unless the cartridge needs more capacitance.\n\nFind which arm wire is which with an ohmmeter from the headshell pins:\nleft is white (signal) and green (ground), right is red (signal) and black (ground).\nThe wire colours inside the arm are not the headshell colours." (at 30.48 180.34 0) (effects (font (size 1.4 1.4)) (justify left bottom)) (uuid 4de1c336-7086-562d-97c6-719a9f567938))
